# Vector-4D: a 4-component 32-bit-float vector (homogeneous coordinates). Pure float math. `add` / `subtract` combine (it wears `addition` and `subtraction`), `scale` by a scalar, `dot` is the scalar product, `magnitude` the norm, `normalize` the unit vector, `distance` the gap.

mark unstable

load @term/base/float
  find square-root

load @term/base/arithmetic
  find addition
  find subtraction

form vector-4
  link x, like decimal
  link y, like decimal
  link z, like decimal
  link w, like decimal

  wear addition
    task add
      take self
      take other, like vector-4
      like vector-4
      send back
        make vector-4
          bind x
            call add
              read self/x
              read other/x
          bind y
            call add
              read self/y
              read other/y
          bind z
            call add
              read self/z
              read other/z
          bind w
            call add
              read self/w
              read other/w

  wear subtraction
    task subtract
      take self
      take other, like vector-4
      like vector-4
      send back
        make vector-4
          bind x
            call subtract
              read self/x
              read other/x
          bind y
            call subtract
              read self/y
              read other/y
          bind z
            call subtract
              read self/z
              read other/z
          bind w
            call subtract
              read self/w
              read other/w

  # the names before `add` reached a vector (note/term/plan/decisions-2026-10.md, D5), kept for one release
  task plus
    take self
    take other, like vector-4
    like vector-4
    mark deprecated
    back self/add(other)

  task minus
    take self
    take other, like vector-4
    like vector-4
    mark deprecated
    back self/subtract(other)

  task scale
    take self
    take factor, like decimal
    like vector-4
    send back
      make vector-4
        bind x
          call multiply
            read self/x
            read factor
        bind y
          call multiply
            read self/y
            read factor
        bind z
          call multiply
            read self/z
            read factor
        bind w
          call multiply
            read self/w
            read factor

  task dot
    take self
    take other, like vector-4
    like decimal
    send back
      call add
        call add
          call add
            call multiply
              read self/x
              read other/x
            call multiply
              read self/y
              read other/y
          call multiply
            read self/z
            read other/z
        call multiply
          read self/w
          read other/w

  # the norm: `magnitude`, since a collection's `length` counts its items (note/term/plan/decisions-2026-10.md, D2)
  task magnitude
    take self
    like decimal
    send back
      call square-root
        call dot
          read self
          read self

  # the older name of `magnitude`, kept one release
  task length
    take self
    like decimal
    mark deprecated
    back magnitude(self)

  task normalize
    take self
    like vector-4
    save magnitude
      call magnitude
        read self
    send back
      make vector-4
        bind x
          call divide
            read self/x
            read magnitude
        bind y
          call divide
            read self/y
            read magnitude
        bind z
          call divide
            read self/z
            read magnitude
        bind w
          call divide
            read self/w
            read magnitude

  task distance
    take self
    take other, like vector-4
    like decimal
    send back
      call magnitude
        call minus
          read self
          read other

task make-vector-4
  take x, like decimal
  take y, like decimal
  take z, like decimal
  take w, like decimal
  like vector-4
  send back
    make vector-4
      bind x, read x
      bind y, read y
      bind z, read z
      bind w, read w
